%description:

Tcp.keepAliveEnabled:socket-override -- the socket turns keepalive on for its connection.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "keepalive (RFC 9293 section 3.8.4): after keepAliveIdleTime without a
received segment and without data in flight, send a probe without data ...; off by default
(MUST-25); TcpSocket::setKeepAlive() turns it on or off for one connection (MUST-24)".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true), socket-override (the socket of the
application turns keepalive on with the parameter false). The code: TcpAlgorithmBase reads
the value at the open and schedules the keepalive timer at the end of the handshake;
TcpAlgorithmBase::setKeepAlive() takes the place of the value for one connection. This test separates "socket-override" from "off": the value is false, as in "off".

Host under test: host1, with an idle time of 1 s (precondition), whose TcpTestApp connects to
host2 at 0.1 s, sends nothing, and turns keepalive on at 0.15 s. Observation: level 1, a probe
(SEG.SEQ = SND.UNA - 1 = the ISN) comes about 1 s later.

%# parameter: Tcp.keepAliveEnabled
%# class: socket-override
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpKeepAliveEnabledSocketOverride")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000); })
                 .describe("host1 connects to host2"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.15).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().setKeepAlive(true); })
                 .describe("the socket of host1 turns keepalive on"))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early keepalive probe")
              .within(0.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("keepalive probe")
             .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpKeepAliveEnabledSocketOverride compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime = 1s
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpKeepAliveEnabledSocketOverride: PASS
